# Implementation Plan: True Offline-First Business Operation in Akauntme

## 1. Overview & Core Principle

> **"NEPA can take the light. MTN can go down. Your business does not stop."**

This plan transitions Akauntme from a network-dependent web app into a **true offline-first business application**. Local IndexedDB becomes the primary operational data layer for all business operations (sales, expenses, products, stock adjustments, invoices, clients, settings). Connectivity is treated solely as a synchronization channel, not a requirement for business continuity.

When offline, operations complete in milliseconds locally, stock decreases immediately on sales, mutations are saved to a durable transaction queue, and automatic retry-safe synchronization reconciles with the backend when connection is restored.

---

## 2. User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Database Schema Migration**: A migration `add_idempotency_key_to_business_tables` will be run on the Laravel backend to add an indexed, nullable `idempotency_key` column to `sales`, `transactions`, `products`, and `customers`. This enables 100% duplicate-safe, retry-safe offline syncing.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Primary Data Layer Inversion**: The frontend store (`useAppStore`) and React Query hooks (`useTransactions`, `useProducts`, `useInvoices`, `useClients`) will now read from local IndexedDB (`dbService`) on app startup and queries. Backend calls will run in the background to sync and reconcile, meaning the application will boot and function instantly with 0 ms wait time even when completely disconnected.

> [!NOTE]
> **Removal of False Offline Behaviors**:
> - The aggressive 5-second polling loop in `ConnectivityProvider` will be removed.
> - Blocking popups (`ServerOfflineModal`, `ServerOfflineCard`) will be removed from standard workflow.
> - Error messages such as "Network error. Try again" will be replaced by subtle, non-intrusive feedback: *"Saved locally. Will sync when you're back online."*

